  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The Cubs blew the game open in the seventh, and the Yankees couldn't answer.",
    "what_this_means": "Max Fried gave them what they needed. One earned run across five-plus innings, clean enough to win. But the offense never showed up when it mattered. Nine strikeouts. Two runs. Eight hits that added up to nothing. They converted one runner in scoring position out of four chances, and that one came too late to matter. Spencer Jones broke a 1-1 tie with a home run in the seventh, but by then Chicago had already scored three and the game was gone. The bullpen didn't implode. It was already over. This is a team that keeps finding new ways to waste decent pitching. Three-and-a-half games back. That margin gets tighter when you leave this many chances on the field.",
